{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdv3tgExCE4TU6sJsSbUA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**None** — Basket.API contains no integration event handler that updates prices of items already in a customer's basket.\n\nHow I established this:\n\n- Basket.API has exactly one integration event handler: `OrderStartedIntegrationEventHandler` (`src/Basket.API/IntegrationEvents/EventHandling/OrderStartedIntegrationEventHandler.cs:6`), and it deletes the basket rather than repricing it (`src/Basket.API/IntegrationEvents/EventHandling/OrderStartedIntegrationEventHandler.cs:14`).\n- The service's event bus wiring registers only that one subscription: `.AddSubscription<OrderStartedIntegrationEvent, OrderStartedIntegrationEventHandler>()` (`src/Basket.API/Extensions/Extensions.cs:18`). There is no `ProductPriceChanged` subscription in Basket.API.\n- Enumerating every node in the `Basket.API` service turned up no other `IIntegrationEventHandler` implementation and no `ProductPriceChanged*` type in that project.\n\nFor completeness (not the answer, just to show where the price-change event does go): `ProductPriceChangedIntegrationEvent` is raised by Catalog when an item's price is updated (`src/Catalog.API/Apis/CatalogApi.cs:350`), and the only handler for it in the whole solution lives in Webhooks.API — `ProductPriceChangedIntegrationEventHandler` (`src/Webhooks.API/IntegrationEvents/ProductPriceChangedIntegrationEventHandler.cs:3`), which dispatches webhooks and does not touch baskets.\n\nSo the \"update prices of items already in the basket\" behavior (present in older eShopOnContainers versions) does not exist in this codebase's Basket.API."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425,"cache_read_input_tokens":9460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":425},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"stand